[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     2[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     3[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Axes derived mechanically from the C source
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     4[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     5[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `c_src/include/lib.h` declares the complete public API — a single entry point:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     6[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     7[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```c
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     8[0m:[38;5;10m[49m float ldexp_q2(float y, int exp_q2);
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     9[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    10[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    11[0m:[38;5;10m[49m There is no context/handle struct, no option setter, no mode flag, no
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    12[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `#ifdef`, no `switch`, and no `if` statement in `c_src/src/lib.c`. There is also
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    13[0m:[38;5;10m[49m no "convenience wrapper vs. low-level" split: `ldexp_q2` *is* the lowest-level
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    14[0m:[38;5;10m[49m entry point, and it is the only one. So the configuration surface is entirely
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    15[0m:[38;5;10m[49m the cross-product of the **input shapes the arithmetic branches on**:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    16[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    17[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Axis 1 — the clamp `e = min(exp_q2, 120)` (`30 * 4`), which determines the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    18[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **iteration count** of the `do`/`while`:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    19[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `exp_q2 <= 0` → 1 iteration, `e = exp_q2` (unclamped, negative or zero)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    20[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `1 <= exp_q2 <= 120` → 1 iteration, `e = exp_q2` for `< 120`, `e = 120` at 120
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    21[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `exp_q2 > 120` → `ceil(exp_q2 / 120)` iterations, last one with the residual
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    22[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    23[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Axis 2 — the table index `e & 3`, selecting which of the four `g_expfrac`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    24[0m:[38;5;10m[49m entries is used: residues `0, 1, 2, 3`. For negative `e` this is the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    25[0m:[38;5;10m[49m two's-complement `&`, so it still lands in `0..=3` but pairs a *negative*
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    26[0m:[38;5;10m[49m quarter-step with a table entry chosen from the low bits.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    27[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    28[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Axis 3 — the integer factor `1 << 30 >> (e >> 2)`, with the shift count masked
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    29[0m:[38;5;10m[49m to 5 bits by the hardware:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    30[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `e >= 0` → count `e >> 2 ∈ 0..=30` → factor `2^30 .. 2^0` (never 0)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    31[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `e < 0` → count `(e >> 2) & 31` → factor aliases with period 128 in `e`;
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    32[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   count `31` (i.e. `e ∈ [-4,-1] mod 128`) makes the factor **0**
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    33[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    34[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Axis 4 — the `float y` shape (the value-dependent axis; `f32` multiplication is
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    35[0m:[38;5;10m[49m neither associative nor exact, so magnitude class matters):
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    36[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * normal positive / normal negative
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    37[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `+0.0` / `-0.0`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    38[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * subnormal (positive and negative)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    39[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `FLT_MIN`, `FLT_MAX`, `FLT_EPSILON`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    40[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `+inf` / `-inf`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    41[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `NaN` (default quiet, negative-sign, and non-default payload)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    42[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * fully random `f32` bit patterns (all classes mixed)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    43[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    44[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Axis 5 — the multiplication ORDER, fixed by the C source and verified in the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    45[0m:[38;5;10m[49m disassembly (`mulss %xmm1,%xmm0` = `frac * (float)shifted` first, then
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    46[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `mulss` with `y`). Not a free axis, but every row asserts it implicitly since a
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    47[0m:[38;5;10m[49m reassociated Rust version diverges in the low mantissa bit.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    48[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    49[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Axis 6 — feature combinations. `translation/Cargo.toml` declares **no
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    50[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `[features]` section**, so the only configuration is the default (empty) feature
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    51[0m:[38;5;10m[49m set; `--no-default-features` is equivalent. Recorded in row 25.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    52[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    53[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Axis 7 — binary/driver executable. Neither `c_src/CMakeLists.txt` (it only
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    54[0m:[38;5;10m[49m does `add_library(... SHARED src/lib.c)`) nor `translation/Cargo.toml`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    55[0m:[38;5;10m[49m (`crate-type = ["cdylib"]`, no `[[bin]]`, no `src/main.rs`) builds an
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    56[0m:[38;5;10m[49m executable. The "compare stdout of the C and Rust binaries" step is therefore
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    57[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **N/A**; recorded in row 26.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    58[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    59[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Configuration rows
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    60[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    61[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Every row is exercised through **both** `.so` files via `libloading`, with many
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    62[0m:[38;5;10m[49m randomized inputs per row (fixed-seed SplitMix64 PRNG), and compared on raw
